## Setup
Let $\alpha := 1.1$, $\beta := 0.4$, $\delta := 0.1$ and $\gamma := 0.4$, with $\alpha \in [0.5, 2]$ and $\gamma \in [0.1, 1]$.

$$ \dot x = \alpha x - \beta x y, \quad \dot y = \delta x y - \gamma y, \quad x(0) = 10, \ y(0) = 5 $$

## Equilibrium
$$ \operatorname{solve}_{x, y} \big(\alpha x - \beta x y = 0,\ \delta x y - \gamma y = 0,\ x > 0,\ y > 0\big) = ? $$

## Conserved quantity
$$ V(x, y) := \delta x - \gamma \ln x + \beta y - \alpha \ln y $$
$$ \frac{d}{dt} V\big(x(t), y(t)\big) = ? $$
$$ \max_{t \in [0, 50]} \frac{|V(t) - V(0)|}{|V(0)|} \approx ? $$

Figure: $x(t)$ and $y(t)$, $t \in [0, 50]$.
